# Control server transport owner: services/control/internal/platform/config/server_transport.go.
# Copy selected keys to one existing protected0600 single-link serve --env-file; no ambient authority.
# This complete selection is direct HTTPS. Keep the base YAML independently valid before overrides.
# A transport change requires matching YAML: remove contradictory TLS/proxy fields from both sources.
# Empty values do not unset fields. No shell expansion, source rebuild, live reload or provider-TLS switch.

# Owner server.transport_mode; optional string enum http/direct_https/trusted_proxy_https.
# Omission retains legacy direct_https; this explicit enum overrides valid YAML and requires restart.
# Public nonsecret setting. HTTP is plaintext; proxy mode requires its separately protected TLS proxy.
PROJECT_ONE_TRANSPORT_MODE=direct_https

# Owner server.listen_address; required string host:port, canonical port1..65535, bracket IPv6.
# No listener default; explicit env-file overrides valid YAML; restart rebinds the listener.
# Public nonsecret bind, separate from browser origins; 0.0.0.0/[::] are bind-only, never destinations.
# This example selects loopback; use an explicitly isolated bind/projection for a real proxy backend.
PROJECT_ONE_LISTEN_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1:8443

# Owner server.portal_origin; required canonical http/https origin string, no path/query/fragment/userinfo.
# No default; match the selected mode and actual chosen DNS/localhost/IP plus effective port1..65535.
# Public nonsecret origin; explicit env-file overrides valid YAML; restart and callback/session reconciliation.
# DNS must be lowercase, IPv6 bracketed; omit default80/443. Never rewrite localhost to an IP alias.
PROJECT_ONE_PORTAL_ORIGIN=https://portal.example.invalid:8443

# Owner server.admin_origin; required canonical origin string with the same scheme as Portal/mode.
# No default; must be a distinct origin. Port does not isolate cookies; audience binding stays required.
# Public nonsecret origin; explicit env-file overrides valid YAML; restart/callback/session reconciliation.
# DNS/localhost/IP is an explicit destination; do not put a wildcard bind address here.
PROJECT_ONE_ADMIN_ORIGIN=https://admin.example.invalid:8443

# Owner server.tls_certificate_file; absolute canonical protected certificate-chain file reference string.
# Required for direct HTTPS serving; no default. Omit in http/trusted_proxy_https, including base YAML.
# Reference only, never certificate/private-key bytes. Startup checks actual pair/validity/DNS or IP SANs.
# Explicit env-file overrides valid YAML; restart required. Normal client chain validation remains required.
PROJECT_ONE_TLS_CERTIFICATE_FILE=/run/projectone/certificate.pem

# Owner server.tls_private_key_file; absolute canonical protected private-key file reference string.
# Required with certificate for direct HTTPS serving; no default. Omit in the other two modes and YAML.
# Secret reference only; key material must pass existing private-file checks, never log or embed it.
# Explicit env-file overrides valid YAML; restart required. Missing material never downgrades to HTTP.
PROJECT_ONE_TLS_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE=/run/projectone/private-key.pem

# Owner server.trusted_proxy_cidrs; JSON array of distinct canonical IPv4/IPv6 CIDR strings, no units.
# Required nonempty only in trusted_proxy_https; absent in direct_https/http. No trust-all/default peers.
# Public nonsecret policy kept out of browser configuration; requires a real isolated single-hop proxy.
# No host bits, zones, mapped IPv4, multicast, unspecified or /0. This line is intentionally inactive.
# Explicit env-file overrides independently valid YAML; restart required. Preserve exact socket-peer checks.
# PROJECT_ONE_TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS='["127.0.0.1/32","::1/128"]'

# CA verification stays with its client/operation. Existing offline trust input:
# PROJECT_ONE_OFFLINE_TLS_TRUST_BUNDLE_FILE belongs to the offline operator request, not serve --env-file.
# Native probe/browser fixture and provider/gateway owners select their own protected CA references.
# Do not pass that offline key to serve, install shared-system trust automatically or skip verification.

# For HTTP, explicitly select http, two http origins and a matching bind; omit both TLS keys and proxy list.
# Current enabled SSO requires HTTPS callbacks and is refused in HTTP; local account recovery is separate.
# For trusted proxy HTTPS, retain two https origins, omit local TLS refs and select a nonempty CIDR list.
# A configuration parse is not full listener/Cookie/browser/deployment acceptance; see deployment-transport spec.
